	<description>&lt;i&gt;Anya could really use a friend. But her new BFF isn't kidding about the "Forever" part.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Of all the things Anya expected to find at the bottom of an old well, a new friend was not one of them. Especially not a new friend who’s been dead for a century.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Falling down a well is bad enough, but Anya's normal life might actually be worse. She's embarrassed by her family, self-conscious about her body, and she's pretty much given up on fitting in at school. A new friend—even a ghost—is just what she needs.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Or so she thinks. Spooky, sardonic, and secretly sincere, &lt;i&gt;Anya's Ghost&lt;/i&gt; is a wonderfully entertaining debut from author/artist Vera Brosgol.</description>
